          "id": "5bb7b848d17ddc07ca1aa607d5e3c41ae1e0d073",
          "message": "feat(importer): apply ChoiceSet rules to every pack, never replace one (#1582)\n\n* feat(importer): never replace a committed pack, only apply rules\n\ncontent-import now writes only with --apply-rules <Key>,...; the full import\nthat overwrote a pack's entry files is gone, as is the restore dance it needed.\nApplying rules keeps each entry's own rules as written, so a re-run adds rules\nwithout reordering the keys of the ones already there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(content): apply ChoiceSet and the rules that read it to every pack\n\nRuns content-import --apply-rules ChoiceSet,GrantItem,Resistance,Weakness,\nImmunity,FlatModifier,DamageDice,ItemAlteration,RollOption,AdjustModifier,\nAdjustStrike,BaseSpeed,CreatureSize,TempHP on all 50 packs. 326 entries gain\n794 rules and nothing else changes: no existing rule, no other field, no new\nbacklog gap. ChoiceSet gaps in the backlogs go from 628 to 431. One prompt's\n\"resistance\" is fixed by the typos hook.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(importer): drop restore tooling and unused pack-writes helpers\n\nRestore only ran after a full import, which no longer exists. Removes\nrestore-additions, restore-merge, the content-restore recipe, and\npackWrites with its helper. Keeps unregistered and missing, which a\ntest uses to check the catalogs against the committed pack files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
